      "task": "Compare all four function-value pairs from fig-52 and identify the decreasing and increasing argument sets.",
      "independent_solution": "The actual styled fig-52 graph has a single bottom turning point at x=0. Moving left to right on the negative-x branch lowers the function value, while moving left to right on the positive-x branch raises it. Thus a) -3.6 < -2.1 < 0 implies f(-2.1) < f(-3.6); b) 0 < 1.3 < 2.8 implies f(1.3) < f(2.8); c) x1 < x2 < 0 implies f(x1) > f(x2); d) 0 < x1 < x2 implies f(x1) < f(x2). The decreasing argument set is x<0, and the increasing argument set is x>0; adjoining x=0 gives the valid maximal closed-ended half-lines (-infinity,0] and [0,infinity), respectively. This is a reading of branch order, not an assumption that the curve is exactly x^2, even, or has a specified minimum height. The stated full domain R remains unchanged."
    },
    {
